narrative:
## Building a Tip Calculator

This is your L1 showcase project — a complete tip calculator built entirely with functions. Each function handles one part of the calculation, and main ties it all together.

### The Calculator Design

```xiom
fn calc_tip(amount: Int, percent: Int) -> Int {
  return amount * percent / 100;
}

fn calc_total(amount: Int, tip: Int) -> Int {
  return amount + tip;
}

fn print_bill(amount: Int, percent: Int) {
  let tip: Int = calc_tip(amount, percent);
  let total: Int = calc_total(amount, tip);

  io.println("=== RESTAURANT BILL ===");
  io.println("Bill amount: $");
  io.println(amount);
  io.println("Tip (");
  io.println(percent);
  io.println("%): $");
  io.println(tip);
  io.println("Total: $");
  io.println(total);
}

fn main() {
  print_bill(80, 15);
}
```

Three functions working together:
- `calc_tip` — calculates just the tip amount (amount × percent ÷ 100)
- `calc_total` — adds the tip to the bill for the total
- `print_bill` — orchestrates everything: calculates, formats, and prints

This is how real programs work — small, focused functions that call each other. Change the bill to $120 with a 20% tip by editing just two numbers in `main`!

